# The sdist must be self-testable: downstream packagers (conda-forge, Debian,
# Fedora, Nix, Spack) build from it and run the suite against their own NumPy /
# SciPy. setuptools' legacy default picks up ``test*.py`` only, which drops the
# test package init, its helpers and its fixture CSVs — the shipped tests then
# fail to import. Wheels stay test-free (packages are found under src/).
include CHANGELOG.md
include LICENSE
recursive-include tests *.py
recursive-include tests/data *.csv *.json
recursive-include scripts *.py
# Synthetic seed configs/CSVs: the Loewe suite fits them directly.
recursive-include data *.json *.csv
global-exclude __pycache__/* *.py[cod]
prune AGENTS.md
